From a14eab541340ecd637d45d5c2c918e951003c24d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tatsuki Tanaka <tatsuki@tanakatatsuki.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:20:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 45/46] ASoC: qcom: q6apm-voice: drop and free PCM on backend
 close

When tearing down hostless voice backend sessions, ensure the underlying
PCM stream drops pending frames and frees allocated hardware resources
before releasing the substream reference.

Signed-off-by: Tatsuki Tanaka <tatsuki@tanakatatsuki.dev>
(cherry picked from commit ed120558cd2c5f970edc44e1273a8d7b6caed825)
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-voice-backend.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-voice-backend.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-voice-backend.c
index 9aee99533da4..43b11caf8e99 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-voice-backend.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-voice-backend.c
@@ -24,6 +24,8 @@ void q6apm_voice_backend_close(struct snd_pcm_substream **stream)
 
 	if (!substream)
 		return;
+	snd_pcm_kernel_ioctl(substream, SNDRV_PCM_IOCTL_DROP, NULL);
+	snd_pcm_kernel_ioctl(substream, SNDRV_PCM_IOCTL_HW_FREE, NULL);
 	guard(mutex)(&substream->pcm->open_mutex);
 	snd_pcm_release_substream(substream);
 	*stream = NULL;
